\begin{proof}
Since $|G|=312=2^3\cdot3\cdot13$, a Sylow $13$-subgroup has order $13$. Let $n_{13}$ be the number of Sylow $13$-subgroups. By Sylow's theorems, $n_{13}$ divides $24$ and satisfies $n_{13}\equiv1\pmod{13}$. Among the divisors of $24$, only $1$ is congruent to $1$ modulo $13$ (the next possibility, $14$, does not divide $24$). Thus $n_{13}=1$. Therefore the Sylow $13$-subgroup is unique, and every unique Sylow subgroup is normal. Hence $G$ has a normal Sylow subgroup.
\end{proof}
